# No registry binding is committed for the @webbpulse scope.
#
# This repository never resolves @webbpulse packages from the registry: the
# workspaces link to each other locally. A committed binding would also take
# precedence over the user level configuration that
# `aws codeartifact login --tool npm` writes, so the publish workflow would see
# a placeholder instead of the CodeArtifact endpoint.
#
# Consumer applications bind the scope themselves. Either run
#
#   aws codeartifact login --tool npm --domain webbpulse \
#     --domain-owner <artifacts account id> --repository npm --region us-west-2
#
# or commit the equivalent pair in their own .npmrc with the values read from
# the environment (see the README).
